 "context": "<figure id=\"fig-ch33_03_02\" class=\" \"><span data-type=\"media\" id=\"fs-idp90821984\" data-alt=\"Prior to birth, the baby pushes against the cervix, causing it to stretch. Stretching of the cervix causes nerve impulses to be sent to the brain. As a result, the brain stimulates the pituitary to release oxytocin. Oxytocin causes the uterus to contract. As a result, the baby pushes against the cervix in a positive feedback loop.\">\n<img src=\"https://openstax.org/apps/archive/20241024.164013/resources/fd103c51c5aea33964d6de38142e21514a0b01d5\" data-media-type=\"image/png\" alt=\"Prior to birth, the baby pushes against the cervix, causing it to stretch. Stretching of the cervix causes nerve impulses to be sent to the brain. As a result, the brain stimulates the pituitary to release oxytocin. Oxytocin causes the uterus to contract. As a result, the baby pushes against the cervix in a positive feedback loop.\" width=\"270\" height=\"253\">\n</span>\n</figure>",
 "stimulus_html": "",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 521019,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p>State whether each of the following processes is regulated by a positive or negative feedback loop.</p>\n<p> a. A person feels satiated after eating a large meal.</p>\n <p>b. The blood has plenty of red blood cells. As a result, erythropoietin, a hormone that stimulates the production of new red blood cells, is no longer released from the kidney.</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1018385,
     "content_html": "<p>a. This is regulated by a positive feedback loop as the stimulus (hunger) has changed direction in response to a signal (fullness).</p>\n <p>b. This is regulated by a positive feedback loop as the stimulus (red blood cell release) has changed direction in response to a signal (presence of enough red blood cells).</p>"
    },
    {
     "id": 1018386,
     "content_html": "<p>a. This is regulated by a negative feedback loop as the stimulus (hunger) has changed direction in response to a signal (fullness).</p>\n<p> b. This is regulated by a positive feedback loop as the direction of the stimulus has been maintained.</p>"
    },
    {
     "id": 1018387,
     "content_html": "<p>a. This is regulated by a positive feedback loop as the stimulus (hunger) has changed direction in response to a signal (fullness).</p>\n<p> b. This is regulated by a negative feedback loop as the stimulus \n (red blood cell release) has changed direction in response to a signal (presence of enough red blood cells).</p>"
    },
    {
     "id": 1018388,
     "content_html": "<p>a. This is regulated by a negative feedback loop as the stimulus (hunger) changed direction in response to a signal (fullness).</p><p> b. This is regulated by a negative feedback loop as the stimulus (red blood cell release) changed direction in response to a signal (presence of enough red blood cells).</p>"
    }
